  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is churchtools_chat, the checkout directory is nextcloud-churchtools-chat.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 31 to 34; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 31 reaches below the oldest maintained major (32), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 24 stated in main-verification.yml, pr-checks.yml, publish-appstore.yml, release.yml, within package.json engines.node ^24.0.0.",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: PHPUnit (phpunit.xml).",
        " No ESLint configuration: nothing checks the frontend sources, so a wrong import is found by the build or not at all.",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No PHP-CS-Fixer configuration: no coding standard is applied to the PHP sources, so formatting is settled in review instead of by a command.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "1 declared package is named nowhere in the checkout: php-parser.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 219 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
